        {
          "id": 1863454357,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "As I remember, 39ed3527a5a85e1f403a998bdb636d9a941cd391 significantly improved performance, but that may not be enough to make it worth backporting if we deem slowness reading large BLF files as a bug.\n\n4e8603b60438650fe3329d5a0a0e8ff0bc96b08c might also have improved performance; see previous comment.\n\n3d6324175638d3be912446c8d171fc9db1cc5234 has the title \"BLF: Fix handling of 0-length log containers\", so it presumably fixes a bug.\n\n8f670352df8551c7c1c68a00b9babb98709756e7 definitely fixes a (crashing) bug.\n\nSo at least some of those should perhaps be backported; if 39ed3527a5a85e1f403a998bdb636d9a941cd391 and 4e8603b60438650fe3329d5a0a0e8ff0bc96b08c shouldn't be, then, if the others should be (they, and this bug, fix the handling of 0-length containers), they should be backported, which may take more work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
